# Protect User Work

- Do not commit, push, amend, rebase, reset, checkout, force sync, or otherwise change Git history unless the user explicitly asks for that exact action.
- Do not overwrite, revert, delete, or reformat unrelated files. Treat every uncommitted change and every untracked file as user-owned unless you created it in the current task.
- Before editing, identify the smallest files needed for the request and keep changes scoped there.
- If a fix requires touching deployed backend, GitHub configuration, or CI/CD, explain the change and get explicit approval before making it.
- When repairing a regression, preserve existing features and data contracts unless the user explicitly asks to replace them.
- Before any website deploy or route/build config change, run `git status --short` and include relevant untracked files in the deployment plan instead of assuming only tracked files matter.
- Preserve standalone presentation/static pages and their route mappings, especially `nike-statskey-presentation.html`, `public/nike-run-club/**`, `public/hospital-ckm/**`, `public/prototype/**`, and `vercel.json` rewrites.
- If a live page is down, fix the route/deploy inclusion directly. Do not solve it by reverting recent website edits or removing newer pages.
